o compensatory plan, preserve clinical guidance, and read with curiosity rather than dread. The resulting state matches the assigned handoff: the reader need not start another diet now and can become curious about ending the debate rather than managing it more perfectly.\n\n## Final verdict\n\n**Assigned transition verdict:** The chapter successfully moves the reader from expecting discipline, deprivation, and permanent negotiation to accepting a low-risk investigation conducted while eating normally. Recognition is specific and nonjudgmental, the managed-truce comparison makes the offered destination concrete, and the chapter does not prematurely attempt the benefit-demolition reserved for later. It clearly frames freedom as the disappearance of BAD SUGAR from the “active decision catalog,” not improved moderation, and lands the instruction after the reader has been given reasons to trust it. All three assigned mantras contribute to the movement rather than appearing as detached slogans.\n\n**Largest momentum loss:** NONE."},"sequence_number":503}

